steps.do:
For an ATM cash discrepancy whose disputed amount (the shortfall) exceeds $200, tell the customer:
- an Electronic Fund Transfer Error Resolution Affidavit will be emailed to their registered email;
- they have 10 business days to sign and return it;
- failing to return it may lead to denial of the claim;
- signing a false affidavit is a federal offense.

For each account, compare the number of fileable disputes (c_prefiling) with its free slots (d_count). If there are more disputes than slots, tell the customer:
- the account has a per-account open-dispute limit;
- how many open disputes it already has;
- how many more can be filed now.
Ask which disputes to file first (info dispute_priority), and file only that many, in the customer's order. Tell them the others can be filed once an open dispute on that account is resolved, as long as each transaction is still no more than 60 days old. If no slots are left, file nothing on that account and explain why.

Confirm each filed dispute and its category. Tell the customer:
- whether provisional credit applies: it is the full disputed amount, reduced by the $50 or $500 liability if reported late, issued within 10 business days of filing (20 for accounts open less than 30 days);
- the investigation timeline: 45 business days with provisional credit; 90 days for international transactions, POS transactions outside the US, or new accounts;
- that if the investigation finds against them, the credit is reversed, with written notice at least 3 business days before.
Name any issue that was not filed, and say why.

If the card's status (a_cards) is ACTIVE, first tell the customer four things:
- new transactions will be declined while the card is frozen;
- recurring payments will be declined too;
- pending authorized transactions may still process;
- they can unfreeze any time through customer service or the mobile app.
Then unlock and call freeze_debit_card_3892 once. If the card is already FROZEN, nothing is needed. If it is in any other status, explain that it cannot be frozen.

Confirm the closure. Tell the customer:
- the card is permanently deactivated and cannot be reactivated;
- recurring payments must be updated with new payment details;
- refunds to the closed card will go to the linked checking account.
For fraud_suspected, also recommend changing the online banking password, and advise reviewing recent transactions and disputing any unauthorized charges. Then go to r_account if the customer wants a replacement.

Check the ordering requirements:
- account_type is checking and status is OPEN;
- the account has been open at least 3 business days (date_opened, excluding weekends);
- there is no ACTIVE card and no PENDING card on the account;
- the balance is at least $25;
- the customer is at least 18 (DOB);
- the address on file is a valid US domestic address.
If any check fails, tell the customer what must be resolved, and do not order.
